	"pba_pocketboy_advance_black": {"stats": [["SERIES", "PocketBoy family"], ["RELEASED", "2003-02-14, 2003-03-23, 2003-03-28"], ["MAKER", "Funtendo"], ["TYPE", "Handheld game console"], ["GENERATION", "Sixth"], ["DISCONTINUED", "Yes; date undisclosed"], ["UNITS SOLD", "42,430,000, 41,920,000, 42,820,000"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "The PocketBoy Advanced SP (GBA SP), released in Japan on February 14, 2003, is a foldable handheld game console developed, released, and marketed by Funtendo that served as an upgraded version of the original PocketBoy Advanced. The \"SP\" in the name stands for \"Special\"."], ["BEHIND THE SCENES", "When Okada first pitched to Funtendo leadership the idea of a small and thin PocketBoy Advanced that used a rechargeable battery, the feedback was almost entirely negative."], ["LAUNCH", "In most other regions it was released in Platinum Silver and Charcoal Black."], ["RECEPTION", "As of June 30, 2009, the PocketBoy Advanced series has sold 81.48 million units worldwide, of which 43.52 million are PocketBoy Advanced SP units."], ["HOW IT PLAYS", "The first PocketBoy Advanced SP had a frontlight that illuminated the front of the display and a reflective surface behind the screen that sent light back through the liquid crystal pixel elements to the viewer."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "In 2003, Toys \"Я\" Us sold an exclusive gold edition (without any Zeldo symbols) in the US starting on Black Friday of that year, initially with a Super Plumber Advanced 4 game."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "In 2006, the AGS-101 backlit model also saw a very limited release in Europe."]], "year": 2003},
