	"pba_pocketboy_micro": {"stats": [["SERIES", "PocketBoy Advance family"], ["RELEASED", "2005-09-13, 2005-09-19, 2005-11-03"], ["MAKER", "Funtendo"], ["TYPE", "Handheld game console"], ["GENERATION", "Sixth"], ["DISCONTINUED", "Yes; date undisclosed"], ["UNITS SOLD", "2,420,000, 1,820,000, 700,000"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "The PocketBoy Micro (stylized as GAME BOY micro) is a handheld game console developed and manufactured by Funtendo. It was first released in Japan on September 13, 2005 as a smaller, lighter redesign of the PocketBoy Advanced."], ["BEHIND THE SCENES", "The system was released in Japan on September 13, 2005, in North America on September 19, 2005, in Australia on November 3, 2005, and in Europe on November 4, 2005."], ["LAUNCH", "As of July 30, 2007, the PocketBoy Micro had sold 2.5 million units, according to PocketBoyPro. The PocketBoy Micro sold over 170,000 units during its first days in Japan."], ["RECEPTION", "The system was originally available in black and silver, and a red 20th Anniversary Edition was later released to commemorate the 20th anniversary of the Funtendo FES."], ["HOW IT PLAYS", "According to Funtendo of America vice president George Harrison, the idea for a smaller version of the PocketBoy was first discussed in 2004."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "The system retailed for US$ 99, compared to US$79 for the PocketBoy Advanced SP."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "The \"20th Anniversary\" edition was released on December 4, 2005, which was the Funicom controller-inspired version released in Japan."]], "year": 2005},
